<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Dec new car sales up 2.45 percent yr/yr.</title>
<headline>S.African Dec new car sales up 2.45 percent yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African new car sales rose 2.45 percent to 17,727 units in December from 23,676 units in November and 17,304 units in the same month a year ago.</p>
<p>The National Association of Automobile Manufacturers of South Africa said this brought year sales to 249,884 against 236,584 in 1995.</p>
<p>    Detailed Sales data:	   Dec 96  Nov 96  Dec 95</p>
<p>    New passenger cars	     17,727  23,676  17,304</p>
<p>    Light commercial vehicles     8,367  10,963   9,100</p>
<p>    Medium commercial vehicles	346     496     238</p>
<p>    Heavy commercial vehicles	 502     664     444</p>
<p>    TOTAL:			     26,942  35,799  27,086</p>
<p>Individual manufacturer car sales:</p>
<p>Toyota 8,088, Volkswagen 4,087, Samcor 3,550, Nissan 2,365, Delta 4,143, Mercedes-Benz 2,397, BMW 1,282, Land Rover SA 364, Daewoo 376, Iveco 69, Tyco 40, MAN 58, Dacia 4, Erf 8, AAD 29, Scania 13, Subaru 4, Freightliner 5.</p>
<p>					    Jan-Dec 96   Jan-Dec 95</p>
<p>    New passenger cars		249,884	 236,584</p>
<p>    Light commercial vehicles     129,575	 128,397</p>
<p>    Medium commercial vehicles	5,457	   4,139</p>
<p>    Heavy commercial vehicles	 8,110	   7,664</p>
<p>    TOTAL:				393,026	 376,784</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
